      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T17:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO, gfxstream host changes should aim to backwards-compatible with existing Android guests and hypervisors, correct? aosp/3323076 changed the default (on the host) from on to off. Based on the code-change, this seems like it may have been unintended (the following code snippit doesn\u0027t make sense, it effectively sets `feature.enabled \u003d feature.enabled`)\n\n```\n    GFXSTREAM_SET_FEATURE_ON_CONDITION(\n        \u0026features, VulkanBatchedDescriptorSetUpdate, features.VulkanBatchedDescriptorSetUpdate.enabled);\n```\n\nI understand the change, and understand the argument that vulkanBatchedDescriptorSetUpdates was a mistake to begin with. But I think we need to keep the feature ON by default, and hypervisors going forward can choose to *disable* by default by internally setting renderer_features string.",
      "parentUuid": "ff8e9919_99d38a53",
      "revId": "82f7407e135b3ac14473f70252d33fcad9d7b44b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
